00:41:22.750 --> 00:41:26.310
From the way she spoke of him, one would have thought that he'd chosen to die young,

00:41:26.310 --> 00:41:29.970
solely in order to keep her short of money. Then there was her...

00:41:30.000 --> 00:41:35.060
Her brother, Philip, she'd always resented the fact that he had the lion's share of her family's money.

00:41:36.180 --> 00:41:39.320
There were so many things she'd have liked to do with her life, she kept telling him things.

00:41:40.050 --> 00:41:44.580
He tried to draw her out on the subject of Emma Wright, but here she was much more reticent.

00:41:45.670 --> 00:41:48.030
However, she did finally come out with an interesting statement.

00:41:48.610 --> 00:41:49.510
Emma had a lover.

00:41:52.360 --> 00:41:53.140
That's not true.

00:41:53.600 --> 00:41:54.600
Surprises you, I suppose.

00:41:55.790 --> 00:41:56.430
How did you know?

00:41:57.310 --> 00:41:58.030
She told me.

00:42:00.120 --> 00:42:01.580
Did she tell you who the man was?

00:42:02.010 --> 00:42:04.800
No. I suppose I shouldn't have talked about her now that she's dead.

00:42:05.370 --> 00:42:08.470
Still, you asked, and now you know why I say that Anne would be better off without her.

00:42:09.220 --> 00:42:10.140
Where's Anne going to live?

00:42:10.560 --> 00:42:11.020
With me.

00:42:11.660 --> 00:42:12.040
With you?

00:42:12.300 --> 00:42:14.040
Oh, don't look so sharp.

00:42:15.000 --> 00:42:17.460
I can't exactly picture you looking after a child.

00:42:17.660 --> 00:42:21.630
Oh, don't be so sure of that. I'm full of unfulfilled maternal instincts.

00:42:22.440 --> 00:42:22.760
Are you?

00:42:24.010 --> 00:42:26.360
No. I've arranged for her to go to boarding school.

00:42:26.540 --> 00:42:28.640
I didn't expect to hear of her again till the summer holidays.

00:42:29.330 --> 00:42:29.970
Come and sit down over there.

00:42:30.000 --> 00:42:31.140
You're such a long way away.

00:42:31.760 --> 00:42:34.190
Is her father satisfied with this arrangement?

00:42:34.450 --> 00:42:34.770
Oh, yes.

00:42:34.870 --> 00:42:36.150
He came with me to make a home for her.

00:42:36.490 --> 00:42:38.210
Do you call sending her to school making a home?

00:42:38.740 --> 00:42:39.800
Now, don't you start on me.

00:42:40.000 --> 00:42:41.220
I've had quite enough trouble for Anne.

00:42:41.380 --> 00:42:42.960
She wants to be allowed to stay on with Emma's mother.

00:42:43.670 --> 00:42:45.610
Philip wants her to be brought up by someone younger, hence me.

00:42:46.020 --> 00:42:46.420
I see.

00:42:47.080 --> 00:42:48.300
When does she start her school?

00:42:49.040 --> 00:42:49.380
Monday.

00:42:50.140 --> 00:42:52.580
I've got her coming to town tomorrow to get her teeth fixed before she goes.

00:42:53.780 --> 00:42:54.490
Sickening responsibilities.

00:42:54.670 --> 00:42:55.390
Philip cannot be helped.

00:42:55.610 --> 00:42:58.030
I presume your trouble will not go entirely unrewarded.

00:42:58.370 --> 00:42:58.750
Oh, no.

00:42:59.150 --> 00:42:59.970
Philip's making me an allowed...

00:43:00.520 --> 00:43:03.550
I shouldn't have taken it on otherwise. Still, it's an awful nuisance.

00:43:03.710 --> 00:43:06.360
Poor little Anne. Don't waste your sympathy on her.

00:43:07.220 --> 00:43:08.480
What time is this dentist's appointment?

00:43:09.380 --> 00:43:10.280
Why are you so interested?

00:43:10.890 --> 00:43:12.830
I was just thinking that you'd be free while she's there.

00:43:13.320 --> 00:43:13.560
So?

00:43:13.800 --> 00:43:16.200
If I were free at the same time, we might meet.

00:43:17.890 --> 00:43:18.730
That's quite a thought.

00:43:20.180 --> 00:43:22.480
Kate was completely unsuspecting when he made an appointment

00:43:22.480 --> 00:43:24.500
to meet her for tea at the Savoy at 4 o'clock.

00:43:25.420 --> 00:43:27.460
He never had any intention of keeping this appointment.

00:43:28.370 --> 00:43:29.230
He had to see Anne.

00:43:30.380 --> 00:43:32.020
And he had to find a way of seeing her alone.

00:43:32.240 --> 00:43:38.580
Why don't you tell me to come and wait for her here, when I've finished with the dentist?

00:43:38.820 --> 00:43:39.500
Come in, will you?

00:43:40.290 --> 00:43:41.390
She's having tea somewhere.

00:43:41.630 --> 00:43:42.990
She's going to pick me up afterwards.

00:43:44.240 --> 00:43:45.120
Will you wait in here?

00:43:46.220 --> 00:43:47.080
I know this wrong.

00:43:58.780 --> 00:43:59.320
Hello, aunt.

00:44:02.400 --> 00:44:03.520
Did the dentist give you a bad sign?

00:44:03.700 --> 00:44:06.020
I was told to wait here for Aunt Kate.

00:44:06.680 --> 00:44:07.080
Is it all right?

00:44:07.220 --> 00:44:07.920
I was expecting you.

00:44:08.220 --> 00:44:09.200
Your hair's growing nicely.

00:44:09.710 --> 00:44:10.590
Oh, it's awful.

00:44:12.280 --> 00:44:17.100
I thought it was about time you and I had a talk about you.

00:44:18.520 --> 00:44:19.860
Do you like the idea of going away to school?

00:44:21.240 --> 00:44:21.920
I don't mind.

00:44:22.830 --> 00:44:25.340
Do you like your Aunt Kate?

00:44:28.180 --> 00:44:28.420
Yes.

00:44:29.150 --> 00:44:29.970
Are you sure about that?

00:44:30.600 --> 00:44:40.800
yes don't you trust me yes not very much why you're asking me all these questions i want to

00:44:40.800 --> 00:44:46.200
help you a long time ago you trusted me with something very important what was that your

00:44:46.200 --> 00:44:52.540
life hand don't you remember yes why did you say at the inquest that there was no one with your

00:44:52.540 --> 00:44:59.320
mother the last time you saw her because there wasn't that's not true though is it

00:45:00.000 --> 00:45:01.180
I don't know what you want me to say.

00:45:01.380 --> 00:45:02.760
Aunt Kate was with her, wasn't she?

00:45:02.980 --> 00:45:03.940
Oh, leave me alone, please.

00:45:04.200 --> 00:45:06.180
What happened between Kate and your mother before the accident?

00:45:06.800 --> 00:45:07.840
It wasn't an accident.

00:45:08.060 --> 00:45:10.140
It was just the same as if I pushed her.

00:45:10.280 --> 00:45:10.580
You?

00:45:10.920 --> 00:45:12.430
It was my fault.

00:45:12.530 --> 00:45:13.230
How could it have been?

00:45:13.540 --> 00:45:14.240
I know it was.

00:45:15.100 --> 00:45:16.200
I sided against Mummy.

00:45:16.590 --> 00:45:18.090
I don't care what happens to me anymore.

00:45:18.270 --> 00:45:19.030
What does she do, Anne?

00:45:19.170 --> 00:45:19.730
You must tell me.

00:45:20.380 --> 00:45:20.980
I can't.

00:45:21.100 --> 00:45:21.480
You must.

00:45:21.540 --> 00:45:22.060
It's important.

00:45:22.320 --> 00:45:23.620
She made me promise not to.

00:45:23.820 --> 00:45:25.900
She said they'll send me to prison if they find out.

00:45:26.100 --> 00:45:26.820
Kate said that?

00:45:27.120 --> 00:45:27.460
Yes.

00:45:27.720 --> 00:45:28.840
Well, she's no right to say it.

00:45:28.900 --> 00:45:29.920
No one can send you to prison.

00:45:30.000 --> 00:45:32.360
If you tell the truth, what happened, Anne?

00:45:32.570 --> 00:45:33.250
You've got to tell me.

00:45:38.430 --> 00:45:40.110
I went up to Mummy's room to say goodnight.

00:45:42.160 --> 00:45:44.220
I've been playing in the garden since tea time.

00:45:44.830 --> 00:45:46.090
I knew Aunt Kate was with Mummy,

00:45:46.210 --> 00:45:47.990
and as I reached the top of the stairs,

00:45:48.110 --> 00:45:49.810
Aunt Kate was coming out of Mummy's room.

00:45:50.090 --> 00:45:53.630
She was angry, and she talked in a very quiet voice to me.

00:45:54.420 --> 00:45:56.720
She said she had something very important to tell me.

00:45:57.480 --> 00:45:58.280
Then she started.

00:45:58.910 --> 00:45:59.970
She said the most horrible...

00:46:02.880 --> 00:46:07.610
There was going to be a divorce, she said, and I'd have to give evidence against Mummy.

00:46:08.230 --> 00:46:12.230
I'd have to tell them in court for Daddy's sake all the awful things Mummy had done.

00:46:13.580 --> 00:46:15.560
I suppose Mummy must have been listening all the time.

00:46:16.310 --> 00:46:19.740
Suddenly she told Aunt Kate to get out of the house. She wouldn't go.

00:46:20.760 --> 00:46:23.580
Mummy told me to come to her room with her, but I wouldn't.

00:46:24.290 --> 00:46:29.160
I don't know why. I was afraid, I suppose, and I believed what Aunt Kate had said.

00:46:30.220 --> 00:46:34.630
I believed then. It was only afterwards I saw how wicked she was.

00:46:36.530 --> 00:46:38.790
Heard mummy slam the door open for which she went back.

00:46:39.090 --> 00:46:41.040
I never saw her again.

00:46:41.220 --> 00:46:43.530
It was all my fault for believing I was Kate.

00:46:44.670 --> 00:46:45.890
No, Anne, it wasn't your fault.

00:46:51.610 --> 00:46:52.870
What in the world happened to you?

00:46:53.090 --> 00:46:54.120
I'm afraid I couldn't make it.

00:46:54.220 --> 00:46:55.320
I can see that. Where have you been?

00:46:55.420 --> 00:46:56.080
I got held up.

00:46:56.390 --> 00:46:58.290
You could have telephoned me. I waited for you over an hour.

00:46:58.350 --> 00:46:59.970
As it happens, I had more important things to do.

00:47:00.000 --> 00:47:05.820
Who do you think you are? I'm not in the habit of paying for my own tea. Come along, Anne.

00:48:29.280 --> 00:48:29.880
Talk to you, Michael.

00:48:30.000 --> 00:48:56.700
it won't take long do you want to say we can't talk down here i realize it was very silly of

00:48:56.700 --> 00:48:59.980
me to be so annoyed with you this afternoon i suppose you were working and couldn't

00:49:00.380 --> 00:49:01.940
Is that what you came to say?

00:49:02.140 --> 00:49:02.480
Yes.

00:49:03.530 --> 00:49:04.370
I just said it now.

00:49:05.740 --> 00:49:05.980
Good night.

00:49:06.830 --> 00:49:08.090
You're still angry with me.

00:49:08.760 --> 00:49:09.540
Please don't be.

00:49:10.110 --> 00:49:11.590
Let's forget about it and be friends.

00:49:12.630 --> 00:49:13.810
I don't want to see you again, Kate.

00:49:14.560 --> 00:49:15.440
Oh, Michael.

00:49:15.880 --> 00:49:17.060
Just because of this afternoon?

00:49:17.420 --> 00:49:18.460
That has nothing to do with it.

00:49:19.500 --> 00:49:20.740
You can't just drop me like this.

00:49:21.220 --> 00:49:21.920
It isn't fair.

00:49:22.780 --> 00:49:23.900
It'll be better for you if I do.

00:49:24.100 --> 00:49:25.480
How can you say that?

00:49:26.220 --> 00:49:27.300
You're fond of me, aren't you?

00:49:28.180 --> 00:49:29.540
Anyway, I'm very fond of you.

00:49:31.420 --> 00:49:33.820
It's silly to punish us both just because you're angry with me.

00:49:36.830 --> 00:49:41.700
Michael, you're not just trying to end things with me out of a misplaced chivalry, are you?

00:49:42.850 --> 00:49:43.890
Misplaced chivalry? What do you mean?

00:49:44.510 --> 00:49:48.730
It just occurred to me that you might think you were being unfair to go on, knowing that you're not free.

00:49:49.490 --> 00:49:55.580
Oh, I see. You mean I'm trying to drop you rather than involve you with a married man, is that it?

00:49:56.150 --> 00:49:56.750
Well, isn't it?

00:49:56.870 --> 00:49:59.980
I'm asking you for the last time.

00:50:01.310 --> 00:50:02.390
Go home before it's too late.

00:50:03.290 --> 00:50:13.640
Michael, I don't care about a lot of silly conventions.

00:50:14.800 --> 00:50:16.740
I want to be with you under any circumstances.

00:50:20.920 --> 00:50:21.480
So you care?

00:50:24.920 --> 00:50:25.880
Well, you shall be.

00:50:33.480 --> 00:50:37.830
She had made up his mind for him. That was the end for Kate.

00:50:38.110 --> 00:50:43.220
He now began to make his plans for the revenge he'd thought of for so long.

00:50:45.390 --> 00:50:47.490
Arranged for his junior to take over his patients.

00:50:48.230 --> 00:50:52.650
And established at the hospital that there was a possibility that he might not be available for the coming fortnight.

00:50:52.810 --> 00:50:55.960
He wanted to be prepared for every emergency.

00:50:56.280 --> 00:50:59.970
If something should go wrong and prevent him carrying out his plan at...

00:51:00.000 --> 00:51:05.210
once. He didn't want his absence to be noticed. He'd left himself with only one

00:51:05.210 --> 00:51:10.630
appointment before his meeting with Kate Howard. This was a routine job of an

00:51:10.630 --> 00:51:17.720
educational major, which he did at regular intervals as a sideline. While he was

00:51:17.720 --> 00:51:23.670
engaged on it, his mind was working out the practical problems which would be

00:51:23.670 --> 00:51:28.920
involved by this plan he'd formulated. It was a Friday night.

00:51:30.220 --> 00:51:31.780
That was going to make things easier for him.

00:51:33.410 --> 00:51:36.110
He'd arranged to pick her up at a lonely part of the embankment.

00:51:37.000 --> 00:51:41.640
On his suggestion, she'd told her friends that she was going away for a few weeks.

00:51:42.200 --> 00:51:46.500
As they drove out of London, he was full of the usual chatter,

00:51:47.640 --> 00:51:50.040
never suspecting for a moment his real feelings towards him,

00:51:51.390 --> 00:51:53.170
until they'd actually arrived at Emma's house.

00:51:53.930 --> 00:51:55.490
She'd no idea where he was taking her.

00:51:56.910 --> 00:51:58.850
The house was for sale. He wanted to see it.

00:51:58.880 --> 00:51:59.920
She

00:52:00.000 --> 00:52:05.640
accepted this explanation he knew that no one would answer the bell because he remembered the

00:52:05.640 --> 00:52:11.590
gardener telling him that he always went over to his sister's place on friday nights the window

00:52:11.590 --> 00:52:19.060
was still broken as he left it on his last visit he followed him upstairs to emma's room and over

00:52:19.060 --> 00:52:27.930
to the window out of which emma had fallen drew the curtains threw open the window then he told her

00:52:27.930 --> 00:52:29.790
that he was the man emma

00:52:30.000 --> 00:52:37.420
had loved. She'd found out that she was responsible for Emma's death, and now she was going to

00:52:37.420 --> 00:52:45.880
die the same way Emma had died. He told her to throw herself out. At the last moment she

00:52:45.880 --> 00:52:58.750
started to scream, then she fell. This was a murder conceived in perfect sanity and faultlessly

00:52:58.750 --> 00:52:59.370
carried out.

00:53:04.030 --> 00:53:06.350
I'm afraid I've taken rather longer with this story than I'd intended.

00:53:06.610 --> 00:53:09.690
I shall have to leave the more general discussion of the subject until next time.

00:53:11.880 --> 00:53:12.820
May I ask you a question?

00:53:15.360 --> 00:53:15.580
Yes.

00:53:16.280 --> 00:53:18.120
I take it that the murderer was never suspected?

00:53:19.760 --> 00:53:20.000
No.

00:53:21.140 --> 00:53:23.860
Police could find no evidence that pointed to anything other than suicide.

00:53:24.680 --> 00:53:27.480
And yet, like all paranoics, he had to tell someone about it.

00:53:29.710 --> 00:53:29.970
I don't...

00:53:30.000 --> 00:53:30.520
I'd get that.

00:53:30.640 --> 00:53:32.230
He told you, presumably.

00:53:34.750 --> 00:53:36.230
Yes, he was a patient of mine.

00:53:37.080 --> 00:53:37.960
In a lunatic asylum.

00:53:39.690 --> 00:53:40.710
No, he was perfectly same.

00:53:41.640 --> 00:53:42.260
Same as I am.

00:53:43.710 --> 00:53:44.690
You didn't mind my asking.

00:53:46.160 --> 00:53:46.700
Not at all.

00:53:46.760 --> 00:53:47.480
It was a good question.

00:55:00.350 --> 00:55:01.010
Have you been waiting?

00:55:01.490 --> 00:55:02.130
I'll take that.

00:55:19.690 --> 00:55:20.170
Where are we going?

00:55:21.180 --> 00:55:21.720
You'll see.

00:55:22.590 --> 00:55:23.450
Oh, what a surprise.

00:55:25.900 --> 00:55:26.920
You went across a red light.

00:55:27.870 --> 00:55:28.250
Did I?

00:55:36.810 --> 00:55:38.210
You hate women who make up in public.

00:55:39.560 --> 00:55:40.600
I've never thought about it.

00:55:41.360 --> 00:55:43.040
So much for that little subject of conversation.

00:55:43.920 --> 00:55:45.140
Perhaps you'd like to talk about it yourself.

00:55:46.420 --> 00:55:47.560
What was your appointment this evening?

00:55:48.450 --> 00:55:50.210
I was giving a lecture on criminology.

00:55:50.720 --> 00:55:52.560
Well, what have you got to say on that subject?

00:55:53.200 --> 00:55:56.380
I told a story about a man who killed a woman for revenge.

00:55:56.900 --> 00:55:58.360
He was carrying things a bit far.

00:55:59.210 --> 00:55:59.810
Mad, I suppose.

00:56:00.440 --> 00:56:01.460
No, he was perfectly sane.

00:56:02.100 --> 00:56:05.440
No, they always have a kink somewhere, those people who do violent things.

00:56:06.270 --> 00:56:07.710
Take my sister-in-law, for example.

00:56:08.860 --> 00:56:09.960
How does she come into the argument?

00:56:10.560 --> 00:56:12.500
She must have been a bit mad to do a thing like that.

00:56:12.760 --> 00:56:13.120
Like what?

00:56:13.780 --> 00:56:14.560
Mitting suicide.

00:56:15.950 --> 00:56:18.950
What makes you say it was suicide? It was an accident. What's the matter?

00:56:20.150 --> 00:56:22.830
I thought for a moment that was that awful chapel near her house.

00:56:23.440 --> 00:56:24.540
We're going to her house.

00:56:25.620 --> 00:56:26.360
Whatever for?

00:56:27.250 --> 00:56:28.550
You said it was up for sale, didn't you?

00:56:28.800 --> 00:56:29.620
Well, so it is.

00:56:30.250 --> 00:56:31.010
I might buy it.

00:56:32.820 --> 00:56:35.260
Well, what a time to choose to go look over a house.

00:56:36.160 --> 00:56:37.080
You must be demented.

00:56:38.880 --> 00:56:49.560
How'd you get?

00:56:49.700 --> 00:56:51.040
Do let's come back in the daytime.

00:56:51.520 --> 00:56:52.500
I want to show you something.

00:56:53.040 --> 00:56:53.720
It won't take long.

00:56:54.530 --> 00:56:55.110
Oh, all right.

00:57:01.850 --> 00:57:06.070
Where are you going?

00:57:06.700 --> 00:57:08.460
I'm looking to see if any of these windows are open.

00:57:08.930 --> 00:57:10.870
That's not necessary. The gardener should be here.

00:57:11.030 --> 00:57:12.620
He's taking care of the place till it's sold.

00:57:18.780 --> 00:57:19.720
Window broken here?

00:57:25.060 --> 00:57:25.960
You're not serious.

00:57:27.440 --> 00:57:28.240
Certainly I am.

00:57:32.910 --> 00:57:34.710
Well, anything to oblige a criminologist.

00:57:34.890 --> 00:57:39.740
A minute, will I turn on the light?

00:57:39.820 --> 00:57:42.370
No, don't do that. It'll spoil the atmosphere.

00:57:45.600 --> 00:57:47.640
Well, which part of the house do you want to see first?

00:57:48.460 --> 00:57:48.820
Upstairs.

00:57:49.820 --> 00:57:51.180
I'd better lead the way. I know the place.

00:57:53.320 --> 00:57:54.880
Imagine anyone ever wanted to live here.

00:57:55.200 --> 00:57:56.200
I've always loathed it.

00:57:56.380 --> 00:57:58.960
I tried to persuade Philip to sell it long ago when he first inherited it.

00:58:06.010 --> 00:58:08.930
That's right. How did you know?

00:58:09.450 --> 00:58:10.390
I've been here before.

00:58:12.760 --> 00:58:13.060
When?

00:58:16.020 --> 00:58:19.510
What really gave you the idea that she had a lover?

00:58:20.940 --> 00:58:21.840
She told me so.

00:58:22.140 --> 00:58:23.060
Now tell me the truth.

00:58:24.200 --> 00:58:24.740
All right.

00:58:24.980 --> 00:58:27.310
I overheard them talking on the telephone.

00:58:27.730 --> 00:58:28.730
I listened on the extension.

00:58:29.030 --> 00:58:29.970
Didn't you recognize them?

00:58:30.000 --> 00:58:46.080
man's voice no but you do now thought you were safe but when she was dead that was the end of

00:58:46.080 --> 00:58:51.320
the matter did you really imagine that i'd accept her death without making every effort to find out

00:58:51.320 --> 00:58:51.840
how it happened

00:59:19.990 --> 00:59:22.730
Oh, no, I wasn't here.

00:59:22.870 --> 00:59:26.370
You tried to get money out of her because you thought she was being unfaithful.

00:59:27.920 --> 00:59:29.840
And when that was no good, you poisoned the child's mind against it.

00:59:31.850 --> 00:59:35.760
You might just as well have killed it yourself, and just as guilty this way.

00:59:35.920 --> 00:59:44.590
Who's that for?

